  "title": "Shang oracle-bone inscriptions at Anyang",
  "summary": "At Yinxu, the late Shang capital near Anyang, diviners carved questions to royal ancestors on ox bones and turtle shells. More than 150,000 inscribed pieces bearing over 4,500 distinct characters have been found; they record sacrifices, wars, farming and officials, and form the earliest known formal Chinese writing. Scholars first noticed them in 1899.",
